# thoth_tool_classification

Manages `/:tenant-id/thoth/tool-classifications`. Each resource declares the
effects of one exact tool name, such as `read` or `delete`. The enforcer
classifies calls to that tool from this declaration; request bodies cannot set
classes. An exact-action declaration still takes precedence.

Optional `agent_id` limits a declaration to one agent. Tenant-wide effects still
apply: agent declarations add classes and cannot erase tenant-level risk classes.
Changing `agent_id` replaces the declaration.

Changes require a tenant admin, or an approver when the tenant has no admin, with
recent MFA. A control-plane API key needs the `write` permission. A change governs
decisions within 5 seconds of the write.

## Example Usage

```terraform
resource "thoth_tool_classification" "read_orders" {
  tool_name = "orders.list"
  classes   = ["read"]
}

resource "thoth_tool_classification" "delete_order" {
  tool_name = "orders.delete"
  classes   = ["delete"]
}
```
